WEBVTT

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:08.900
E-Excuse me.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:10.860
<b>Club Application</b>

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.810
We saw your article 
in the paper and your website!

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:16.010
You guys are the best! Please let us join you!

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.830
Oh, uh... You want to join the team?

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.280
Wait. Why are you asking me?

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.310
Aren't you the coach?

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:24.980
What?

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:39.970
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.890
You can clear away all the ash you want,

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:06.260
but the road to anti-aging is long. Right?

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:07.940
Shut up.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.510
I appreciate their enthusiasm, though.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.400
I put up a note.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.360
<b>To individuals wishing to join the Kansei University Long Distance Track and Field Team
The Kansei University Long Distance Track and Field Team is not currently recruiting new members.
Please accept our apologies.
We appreciate your understanding.</b>

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:15.080
We'll continue rejecting applicants.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.300
Aotake is full right now,

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.070
and I don't want to be influenced
by any passing fads.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.550
I don't have time to look after new members,

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.080
and I want to focus on the ten of us.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.960
If anyone approaches you at school, 
politely turn them down.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.610
Okay.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.130
We're drowning in interview requests, too.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.880
Choose carefully from the offers
and reject as many as you can.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.940
What? But we could be famous.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.140
Shouldn't you be looking for a job?

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:45.150
I can only assume he's
trying not to think about it.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.740
What about Nippon TV?

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:49.310
We'll continue doing whatever
we started before the qualifier.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:51.350
Got it. Oh, right.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.360
Can we discuss water station
staff and volunteers later?

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.320
Of course.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:00.810
I'm also thinking about checking
out the course next weekend.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:05.180
We can't run it, but it's
worth just looking at it.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.490
Keep your schedules open.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:08.090
Let's go to the hot springs on the way back.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:08.850
What?

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.080
Question.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:13.400
We can't. We have plans that day.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.720
We're playing soccer with 
some friends from language class.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:17.750
Cancel your plans.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.170
What? But they won't have enough players.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.730
We'd be inconveniencing them.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:24.300
There's still time. Find some substitutes.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:28.000
Not even professionals
can afford to run unprepared.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.250
Besides, soccer? What if you got injured?

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.240
Hakone comes first. Don't forget that.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.150
Hey, listen.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.810
Is there any point in obsessing over it?

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:46.410
You've been tricking us, haven't you?

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:51.490
When you recruited us,
you said we'd aim for the top!

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:52.690
That's impossible!

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:54.380
Just look at our time! It's clear as day!

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.840
<b>Shinsei University 10:15:21
Kanagawa International University 10:16:03
Kansei University 10:16:43
Oka University 10:17:44
Yakuo University 10:19:52</b>

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:58.490
No matter how hard we try, we're not
strong enough to beat the seeded teams!

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:00.030
It's impossible for us to win!

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:04.930
You knew that and wheedled us
anyway, didn't you?

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:10.180
You're right that I said we'd aim for the top.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:10.890
But—

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.470
See? See?

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:14.920
Wait. Calm down.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:19.810
Is it really impossible for us to win 
no matter how hard we try?

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:21.110
It's impossible.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:24.280
The twins are right. Our time proves it.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:29.240
Especially in long distance,
it's rare to see an upset.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:33.390
Even Rikudo's second team
is way better than us.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:36.210
You guys knew.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.190
That's not fair!

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.590
But, depending on how 
you look at it, we're lucky.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:49.560
No matter how fast you are, only a
handful of runners get to run at Hakone.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:54.020
But we made it through the qualifier.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.620
We get to run at Hakone, just like we wanted.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:01.980
There are plenty of people
who'd be jealous of that alone.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:04.700
You're not wrong, but...

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.850
There's no point if we can't win!

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:10.910
Yeah! There's no point in competing
when you already know the outcome!

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.620
Then you shouldn't be playing soccer.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:17.290
If you want to win, you should be training.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.300
You think you're so great.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.920
We're saying we can't find
the motivation to do that!

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:26.010
Yeah! How can you say that after
you couldn't respond the other day?

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.460
Enough, guys.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:33.970
If you guys can't run because you can't win,

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:37.220
will you quit living 
because you'll die someday?

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:39.440
Is that how it is? It is, isn't it?

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.690
What are you trying to say?

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.520
Here he goes again.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:45.660
Kakeru's making ridiculous arguments again.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.780
I'll never die. Never.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:52.740
Quibble, quibble. Here comes the quibbler.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.060
To be or not to be? That's the question.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:56.500
But I'll never die.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.750
Listen to me! What are you doing?

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:03.170
Kakeru the quibbler will never die.

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:02.210
What are we doing right now?

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:10.140
I thought you had a question for me.

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:17.520
You're right that I mentioned the top, 
but I didn't mean we'd win.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.480
What did you mean, then?

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.390
I'm searching for that answer, too.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:27.010
I'm searching for the destination.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.170
What it means to run.

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:32.570
This is stupid.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.580
Hey, wait.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:37.400
Kakeru, it's your turn to do the dishes.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:38.410
Why?

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.630
Just because. Learn to keep your cool.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:48.590
Searching for the Answer

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:58.270
Haiji.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:00.230
<b>Chikusei-so</b>

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:00.230
The twins aren't here.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.330
They actually blew us off.

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:04.690
I'm sorry.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.090
It's because I couldn't answer them.

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:12.550
On the way home from the qualifier,
they asked me why we're running.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:19.340
Yeah, but it's like not being able to tell
someone what the meaning of life is.

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:22.080
Nice quibble.

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:27.420
We made it through the qualifier.
We're running at Hakone together.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:31.340
Maybe we've already achieved
the first goal we set for ourselves.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:34.680
But that wasn't the real top.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.610
I knew that, too.

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:40.830
After all, I wanted to aim even
higher with you guys.

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:43.730
But I hesitated to answer them.

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:45.770
Kakeru...

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:04.300
We haven't played soccer in forever.

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:05.150
Yeah.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:08.090
We've just been running this whole time.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:09.800
Yeah.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.420
Do you regret it?

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.050
Choosing this.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:18.510
Nah.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:21.400
We made these plans first.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.700
You're right. We're running at Hakone.

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:28.070
Now we just have to practice
enough that they won't complain.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:29.280
Complain?

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:29.980
Huh?

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:34.200
So who won't complain? Haiji?

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:38.490
The guys who didn't qualify?

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:39.530
Oh...

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:43.930
I hope everyone shows up soon.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:46.250
We got in the habit of waking up early.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:48.630
Joji! Jota!

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:52.010
Let's go!

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:53.970
Who is that?

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:56.430
Hakone!

00:08:57.860 --> 00:08:59.970
Everyone's waiting!

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:01.910
What's he doing?

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:03.430
Who crashes a soccer game?

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:07.250
Let's go to Hakone!

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:09.110
Crap! Let's run!

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.960
But he's one of the best in the country!

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:13.010
He's running at us while smiling!

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:14.670
Stay away!

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:15.790
It's no use! He's catching up!

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:17.270
Jota! Don't give up!

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:34.890
Nicely done.

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:37.930
There's no way you were outrunning him.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:40.680
I can't run anymore...

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.430
I don't consent to this...

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:48.310
<b>Section 1 Starting Line Yomiuri Shimbun Tokyo Office</b>

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:52.730
This is the starting line.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:55.530
The day of the race, the crowds 
on the sidewalk will be a hundred deep.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:58.990
They'll build a huge stage out front,
and cameras will be pointed at the runners.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:00.660
It's a truly grand occasion.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:03.370
Will we have time to think about that?

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:05.620
It's not for the sensitive.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.410
The wind between the buildings is fierce.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.250
Our bodies will get cold quickly.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:12.920
Twenty-one runners will 
begin running amidst the crowd,

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:17.260
thinking only of delivering their sash
to their teammate waiting far ahead.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.670
Let's keep moving.

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:29.770
<b>Section 2 (Section 10) Tsurumi Relay Station</b>

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:35.370
Don't they stop all the traffic here
and turn this into part of the course?

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:36.610
That's amazing.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:39.460
It's way too much pageantry
for a bunch of college students.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:41.830
It means it's worth just that much.

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:44.790
Our running should be worthy of that.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:45.630
Got it.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:51.350
Have you gotten better at driving?

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.790
You're right.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:56.200
I couldn't believe it, but you have, haven't you?

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:59.530
It's not fair for me to only
expect you guys to grow.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:00.760
Hey, cut that out.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:05.100
If you don't keep sucking at driving, 
we won't be able to make excuses anymore.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:08.770
By the way, last year in this section 2,

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:14.370
Kofu's Iwanki and Rikudo's
Fujioka put on a legendary sprint.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:16.740
The Glorious Section 2, huh?

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:18.890
They call it the ace's section.

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:19.790
Kakeru.

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:22.240
Do you want to run it?

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:27.740
No matter the section,

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:31.250
as long as there's a road,
I'll run as hard as I can.

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:35.390
Did you hear that?

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:37.500
He said as long as there's a road.

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:42.560
Was what I said really that weird? Huh?

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:46.330
Oh, no. Your words were encouraging.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:49.270
<b>Section 3 (Section 9) Totsuka Relay Station</b>

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:52.940
<b>Shonan Bridge</b>

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:56.400
Yeesh.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.010
The sea breeze is strong.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.260
It feels nice.

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:03.280
Yeah.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:04.490
<b>Section 4 (Section 8) Hiratsuka Relay Station</b>

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.410
<b>Section 5 (Section 7) Odawara Relay Station</b>

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:10.820
Hey!

00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:12.790
We're finally here.

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.970
It's steeper than I imagined.

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:28.890
Going up this will be hell,

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:31.780
but this means the downhill
is no joke, either, right?

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:32.720
That's right.

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:34.430
Naturally, the strength of your
legs are important in this section,

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:36.900
but your courage and
intelligence matter, as well.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.070
<b>National Route 1 Summit Level</b>

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:40.070
Huh?

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:41.710
This is the highest point?

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.100
So the finish line isn't at the top.

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:49.660
We're almost at the finish
line of the first half.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:52.540
Let's enjoy the scenery while we can.

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:58.040
<b>First Half Finish Line (Section 6 Starting Line) Lake Ashi</b>

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:04.220
Beautiful...

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:09.040
This is awesome.

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:12.090
The air at Aotake doesn't compare to this.

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:15.320
That was mostly your fault.

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:19.200
I wonder what it'll be like
the day of the race.

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:21.570
There will be screaming crowds, right?

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:24.030
Guys.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:28.650
In the parking lot...

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:33.950
You're so eager. You're
even previewing the course.

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:38.080
I'm sorry I called you plebs once.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:41.550
Should you be loafing around here?

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.800
I'm waiting for Group B to arrive.

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:45.940
I'm in Group A.

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:47.430
He's a regular?

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:48.260
Yeah.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:50.490
Oh, yeah. That qualifier.

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:53.670
It's amazing that you were
neck and neck with Iwanki.

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:56.230
I bet you could run the real thing right now.

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:57.940
That's not true.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:00.110
So modest.

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:02.570
What are you guys doing?

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:04.780
You're all here.

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:07.450
We were just talking...

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:11.870
...about what I'd do if I were a Kansei runner.

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:17.210
I mean, no matter how much you
practice, you only have ten runners.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:20.080
If even one of you caught a cold...

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:29.440
And even if you run like crazy
and finish in the top ten,

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:32.140
your oldest runners will graduate.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:38.000
There's no point in earning a seed for 
next year if you don't have enough runners.

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:43.700
Don't you wonder what you're running for?

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:48.920
It must be hard to stay motivated.

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:50.610
Hey, Sakaki!

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:52.790
Group B is here!

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:53.580
Got it!

00:14:55.300 --> 00:14:58.250
See you somewhere on the course.

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:02.460
You sure you guys aren't
connected by a red string of fate?

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:04.920
In some ways, he's diligent.

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:06.650
Don't mind him.

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:09.570
Consider it progress that no one responded.

00:15:12.020 --> 00:15:13.680
I can't!

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:16.640
I am bothered!

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.870
Why didn't you talk back to him?

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:22.320
Tell us why you run!

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:25.820
I told you, I'm searching 
for that answer right now.

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:34.370
Let's go somewhere else.

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:41.950
Sakaki was probably trying to say

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:46.570
that improving yourself by competing
against strong runners from strong schools

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:49.530
is how an athlete should be
and is a reason to run.

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:53.030
But is he right?

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:56.730
Can you say what we're doing is wrong?

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:03.520
It's true that we need every one of us. 
There's no arguing that.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:06.470
I don't know what will happen
next year or the year after that.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:09.830
I'm sure those who empathize
with us will follow.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:14.000
All I can do is believe in that 
and run as hard as I can right now.

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:18.680
So there's no need to respond to him.

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:22.460
All we can do is acknowledge his points
and move forward despite them.

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:26.380
Does that answer your question?

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:31.970
I don't know.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:32.970
But...

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:36.090
We like what you have to say.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.680
Like, huh?

00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:43.300
That feels like enough to me.

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:45.170
Don't be swayed by your emotions.

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:46.650
Debate until you're satisfied.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:49.610
The twins aren't theorists like you.

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:12.090
You had a fight?

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.180
I wouldn't call it a fight.

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:16.480
I understand what he's trying to say, but...

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:21.260
I want to accept what he's saying,
but it feels like he tricked us.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.790
I know what you mean. Haiji is so calm.

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:29.940
Yeah. We missed our opportunity
to return to normal.

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:33.230
It's not like we were wrong, right?

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:38.700
I think you should believe him.

00:17:41.150 --> 00:17:44.810
He's been patiently thinking for four years.

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:48.160
I can believe him because he's come this far.

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:51.840
Compared to all the time
Haiji has spent on it,

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:55.510
our next two months will fly by in a moment.

00:17:57.190 --> 00:18:00.330
And that moment could change your life,

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:02.720
even if you don't understand
anything right now.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:04.720
You're right.

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:07.020
The last six months flew by, too.

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:08.940
A lot has happened.

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:11.410
The qualifier, the training camp,
all the track meets.

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:14.170
And we met Hana.

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:18.140
She's been a huge help,
like when Haiji collapsed.

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:20.330
Oh, yeah. I remember that.

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.100
And she always comes to our practices.

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:23.580
Yeah. She's a huge help.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.600
Without Hana, we wouldn't have made it this far.

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:26.760
And she's cute.

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:32.540
Hey.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:34.750
Where did Haiji go?

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:36.230
Huh?

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:39.730
You're asking me?

00:18:39.730 --> 00:18:42.810
I wanted to discuss the roadside
placement of our members.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:46.930
Oh, and the university's
asking us to turn in our forms.

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.520
Whatever. Sorry to have bothered you.

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:51.980
That was close.

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:56.150
I almost asked if he wanted my help.

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:03.910
It's shocking to know we can't win.

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:09.330
But I was saved by Haiji's words.

00:19:10.030 --> 00:19:12.290
All we can do right now 
is run as hard as we can.

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:13.790
He's right.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:23.760
<b>Congratulations Kansei University Long Distance Track and Field Team</b>

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:17.360
My anxieties have been
eliminated completely.

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:21.530
Is there still something bothering you?

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:23.760
No. I agree.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:26.620
But it's frustrating.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:32.020
Sakaki made Jota and Joji anxious,

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:34.440
but the only thing I can do is run.

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:37.400
You're hard on yourself.

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:42.740
Previewing the course made me realize

00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:49.820
that not you or Haiji, but<i> I</i> have
to finish some section of it.

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:53.650
I have to do what I can do.

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:56.540
There are things only you can do.

00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:01.340
Believe in us and in yourself.

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:04.210
I will.

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:04.870
<b>Congratulations Kansei University Long Distance Track and Field Team</b>

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:08.600
Hey, it's Kansei's Ekiden guys.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:11.480
Oh, yeah. They were on the news.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:14.210
They've got an exchange student?

00:20:14.210 --> 00:20:17.440
I know. I wish they'd run an all-Japanese team.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:22.010
The school's probably paying
for it to promote themselves.

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:23.270
What are you going to tell them?

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:26.050
I'm fine.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:28.950
But... it's ridiculous!

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:31.400
We're all runners!

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:32.500
Kurahara.

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:38.970
It's been a while.

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:43.550
Fujioka?

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:49.810
<b>University Hospital</b>

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:53.020
Kiyose. Kiyose Haiji.

00:20:57.980 --> 00:20:59.060
Yes.

00:22:40.290 --> 00:22:45.460
Next time: And Then, Morning

00:22:40.560 --> 00:22:42.920
<b>Next time: “And Then, Morning.”</b>
